# Where accounts and auth-gateway send traces and metrics, or that they send none.
# The platform delivers exactly one of two answers, and a process that gets neither
# refuses to start outside a local runtime rather than guess:
#
#   TELEMETRY_STATE=available   the cell has a collector. Also sets
#                               OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT to its OTLP/gRPC address,
#                               e.g. http://otel-collector.otel-collector.svc.cluster.local:4317
#                               (http:// is plaintext because the mesh supplies mTLS;
#                               https:// is TLS).
#   TELEMETRY_STATE=absent      the cell has none. Also sets TELEMETRY_ABSENT_REASON to
#                               say why; an absent cell that does not is refused.
#
# The state decides: the key the state does not use is ignored, and the process logs
# that once.
#
# This profile declares neither the state nor the reason, on purpose. Module defaults
# also reach deployed cells, so either shipped here would be inherited by a cell that
# never set it: a healthy `available` cell would warn about a leftover reason on
# every boot, and a cell that sent `absent` without a reason would pass with a
# reason written for a laptop.
#
# A local run has no cell, so it has no collector, and says so itself: the services
# supply the `absent` state and its reason in code, only when the Codefly runtime is
# `local`. Traces then go to wool's stdout tracer and metrics are not exported. Logs
# always go to stdout. Any other environment, `local-dogfood` included, must deliver
# the state itself (see LOCAL_DOGFOODING.md).
#
# The one assignment below is empty, and is here only so the group exists: a
# composing workspace inherits a group from the key it assigns, and a group with no
# key is met at runtime-init as "no configuration found for observability". An empty
# endpoint is no endpoint, so it neither masks a cell's answer nor triggers the
# leftover-key warning.
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=
